From ec8324b18837a5ffa3270af6252e4533a8cda3d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teal <teal@agents.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:25:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs: name the branches a user must actually check out

README and wiki/Building.md told readers to check out `26.1` and `26.2` for the
26.1.x and 26.2 lines. Those refs on the remote mirror upstream
cabaletta/baritone and contain none of this fork's work, so a reader following
the instructions built upstream Baritone and never learned why it looked
robotic. The fork's three version lines are `26.1x` (Minecraft 26.1.2 declares
26.1.*), `26.2-local` and `26.3`, and those are the names documented now, with a
warning over the upstream mirrors.

Also records in wiki/Building.md that the output jar names the Minecraft version
it was built for, so a reader can tell the three apart from the file name.

No source change.
---
 README.md        | 11 ++++++++---
 wiki/Building.md |  9 +++++++--
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 18d06206..263faff0 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -10,10 +10,15 @@ This is a fork of [Baritone](https://github.com/cabaletta/baritone) focused on m
 
 | Branch | Minecraft | Mod Loader | Status |
 |--------|-----------|------------|--------|
-| `26.1` | 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2 | Fabric | [Release v26.1](https://gitlab.com/international-duck-incorporated/Baritone/-/releases/v26.1) |
-| `26.2` | 26.2 | Fabric | [Release v26.2](https://gitlab.com/international-duck-incorporated/Baritone/-/releases/v26.2) |
+| `26.1x` | 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2 | Fabric | [Release v26.1](https://gitlab.com/international-duck-incorporated/Baritone/-/releases/v26.1) |
+| `26.2-local` | 26.2 | Fabric | [Release v26.2](https://gitlab.com/international-duck-incorporated/Baritone/-/releases/v26.2) |
 | `26.3` | 26.3 | Fabric | [Release v26.3](https://gitlab.com/international-duck-incorporated/Baritone/-/releases/v26.3) |
 
+> **Use the branch names in the table, not `26.1` and `26.2`.** The remote also carries
+> `26.1` and `26.2` refs that mirror [upstream Cabaletta](https://github.com/cabaletta/baritone)
+> and do **not** contain any of the work described below. Checking out `26.2` instead of
+> `26.2-local` builds upstream Baritone, not this fork.
+
 ## Quick Start
 
 Install the mod jar for your Minecraft version, then in-game:
@@ -98,7 +103,7 @@ Download from the [Releases](https://gitlab.com/international-duck-incorporated/
 ```bash
 git clone https://gitlab.com/international-duck-incorporated/Baritone.git
 cd Baritone
-git checkout 26.3   # or 26.1, 26.2
+git checkout 26.3   # or 26.1x, 26.2-local
 ./gradlew build
 ```
 
diff --git a/wiki/Building.md b/wiki/Building.md
index faa783a5..4e71f6a0 100644
--- a/wiki/Building.md
+++ b/wiki/Building.md
@@ -21,10 +21,15 @@ Artifacts are in `dist/`.
 
 | Branch | Minecraft | Checkout |
 |--------|-----------|----------|
-| `26.1` | 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2 | `git checkout 26.1` |
-| `26.2` | 26.2 | `git checkout 26.2` |
+| `26.1x` | 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2 | `git checkout 26.1x` |
+| `26.2-local` | 26.2 | `git checkout 26.2-local` |
 | `26.3` | 26.3 | `git checkout 26.3` |
 
+> Use the branch names above. The remote's `26.1` and `26.2` refs mirror upstream
+> [cabaletta/baritone](https://github.com/cabaletta/baritone) and contain none of this
+> fork's work. The output jar is also named after the Minecraft version it was built for,
+> e.g. `baritone-fabric-26.1.2-<build>.jar`, so check the file name matches your version.
+
